# Three-page quick guide for a thermostat. It gathers what a technical manual usually has:
# a figure with overlaid numbers (a Frame with its Overlay elements on top) and its legend
# beside it (a List of Paragraph with the bold written with Markup: markdown, which the Paragraph
# rule enables), colored notices, numbered steps in Markdown, a wiring diagram,
# a terminal block with aligned columns (a Text with Preformatted: pre, in monospace),
# inline code and tables of specifications and of faults. The heading
# structure gives the PDF outline (bookmarks), and the fault table refers to the diagram with
# {page of: wiring}, the page where it is (also inside Markdown). The sections are numbered Heading 2
# (Numbered: true in styles.stxt: 1 to 8) and their subsections, Heading 3 (3.1, 8.1..., also
# those of a Markdown); the product title declares Numbered: false. A Markdown link refers to the
# specifications section with {number of: specs-heading}. The labels are written in
# lowercase and put in uppercase, spaced out, with Case and Letter spacing.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 64 54 66 54
	Title: Quick guide to the Aire+ T2 thermostat
	Language: en
	Section:
		Page overlay:
			Id: header
			Offset: -34 0 auto 0
			Stack:
				Horizontal: justify
