			Style: banner
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 18 0
			Text: Quick guide
				Typography:
					Size: 8
					Bold: true
					Color: #8FD1CC
					Case: uppercase
					Letter spacing: 1.2
			Heading 1:
				Text: Aire+ T2 Thermostat
				Box:
					Padding: 0
					Border: 0
					Margin: 0
				Typography:
					Color: #FFFFFF
					Numbered: false
			Text: Install it, connect it to the app and program your home in under half an hour.
				Typography:
					Size: 11
					Color: #C7E4E1
				Box:
					Margin: 4 0 0 0
		Stack:
			Id: overview
			Gap: 26
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
			Item:
				Frame:
					Id: device
					Box:
						Width: 250
						Height: 250
					Image: examples/manual/en/thermostat.svg
						Alt: The thermostat seen from the front, with the temperature ring and the status light
						Box:
							Width: 100%
					Overlay:
						Offset: 30 auto auto 184
						Style: badge
						Text: 1
					Overlay:
						Offset: 76 auto auto 124
						Style: badge
						Text: 2
					Overlay:
						Offset: 170 auto auto 70
						Style: badge
						Text: 3
					Overlay:
						Offset: 120 auto auto 190
						Style: badge
						Text: 4
			Item:
				Grow: 1
				Block:
					Heading 2:
						Text: Meet your thermostat
						Box:
							Margin: 0 0 8 0
					List:
						Marker: decimal
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Status light.** Solid green when connected to the network; flashes while pairing.
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Current temperature** of the room, in degrees Celsius.
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Target temperature.** The orange dot marks the one you have chosen.
						List item:
							Paragraph: **Dial.** Turn it to raise or lower the temperature and press it to change mode.
		Heading 2:
			Text: In the box
		Grid:
			Id: contents
			Column sizes: repeat(3, *)
			Gap: 10
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 4 0
			Area:
				Block:
					Style: tip
					Box:
						Margin: 0
					Text: 1 Aire+ T2 thermostat
						Typography:
							Bold: true
					Text: with its wall plate
			Area:
				Block:
					Style: tip
					Box:
						Margin: 0
					Text: 2 screws and 2 wall plugs
						Typography:
							Bold: true
					Text: 3.5 × 30 mm
			Area:
				Block:
					Style: tip
					Box:
						Margin: 0
					Text: 1 quick guide
						Typography:
							Bold: true
					Text: the one you are reading
		Block:
			Id: warning-power
			Style: notice
			Text: Warning
				Style: label
			Text: Installation must be carried out by a qualified person. Before touching any wire, switch off the power at the electrical panel and check with a voltage tester that there is no voltage.
		Block:
			Id: installation
			Heading 2:
				Text: Installation
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 8 0
			Markdown:
				Number markers: decimal
				Content >>
					1. Remove the old thermostat and note which terminal each wire goes to.
					2. Separate the wall plate from the thermostat by gently prying at the bottom.
					3. Screw the plate to the wall, **1.5 m** from the floor and away from drafts and heat sources.
					4. Connect the wires to the terminals following the diagram below and tighten the screws firmly.
					5. Fit the thermostat onto the plate and restore the power: it will switch on by itself.
			Image: examples/manual/en/wiring.svg
				Id: wiring
				Alt: Wiring diagram of terminals L, N, C and NO with the wire colors
				Box:
					Width: 100%
					Margin: 6 0 0 0
			Text: Wiring diagram of the four terminals.
				Typography:
					Size: 8
					Color: #5E7479
				Box:
					Margin: 3 0 10 0
			Heading 3:
				Text: If your installation has no neutral
			Markdown:
				Typography:
					Code font: IBM Plex Mono
				Content >>
					The thermostat can run on batteries in homes without a neutral wire. Leave terminal `N` free and see [section {number of: specs-heading}](#specs) to find out which batteries to use. In that case the screen turns off when it is not touched.
			Heading 3:
				Text: Check the connection
			Paragraph: Once installed, the screen should show the time and the temperature. You can check the state of the terminals from the settings menu, with the following sequence:
			Block:
				Id: terminal
				Style: code
				Text:
					Typography:
						Preformatted: true
					Content >>
						> Settings > Service > Terminals

						L     230 V      [ OK ]
						N     0 V        [ OK ]
						C     closed     [ OK ]
						NO    open       [ OK ]
			Block:
				Style: tip
				Text: Tip
					Style: label
					Typography:
						Color: #134E4A
				Text: If a terminal shows in red, check the wire and repeat the check before closing the cover.
			Heading 3:
				Text: Terminal reference
			Table:
				Id: terminals
				Column sizes: 56 * 100
				Header rows:
					Row:
						Cell: Terminal
						Cell: Function
						Cell: Usual wire
				Body:
					Row:
						Cell: L
							Row header: true
							Style: mono
						Cell: Power supply, live
						Cell: Brown
					Row:
						Cell: N
							Row header: true
							Style: mono
						Cell: Power supply, neutral
						Cell: Blue
					Row:
						Cell: C
							Row header: true
							Style: mono
						Cell: Boiler common contact
						Cell: Gray
					Row:
						Cell: NO
							Row header: true
							Style: mono
						Cell: Normally open contact
						Cell: Yellow
		Block:
			Id: app
			Break:
				Before: page
			Heading 2:
				Text: Connect the app
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 8 0
			Stack:
				Gap: 24
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 8 0
				Item:
					Image: examples/manual/en/app.png
						Id: app-screen
						Alt: The main screen of the app, with the living room temperature and the plus and minus buttons
						Box:
							Width: 112
				Item:
					Grow: 1
					Markdown:
						Number markers: decimal
						Content >>
							1. Download the **Aire+** app from your phone's app store.
							2. Create an account or sign in with the one you already have.
							3. Tap **Add thermostat** and press and hold the thermostat dial for five seconds.
							4. When the light flashes green, choose your Wi-Fi network and enter the password.
							5. Give the room a name, for example “Living room”. Done!

							If pairing fails, bring the phone closer to the thermostat and check that you are using a **2.4 GHz** network: 5 GHz is not supported.
			Heading 2:
				Text: Set your weekly schedule
			Paragraph: The thermostat comes with an energy-saving schedule that you can change from the app or from the dial menu. These are the factory time slots:
			Table:
				Id: schedule
				Column sizes: * * *
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 12 0
				Header rows:
					Row:
						Cell: Time slot
						Cell: Monday to Friday
						Cell: Weekend
				Body:
					Row:
						Cell: Morning · 06:30–08:30
							Row header: true
						Cell: 21 °C
						Cell: 18 °C
					Row:
						Cell: Day · 08:30–17:00
							Row header: true
						Cell: 17 °C
						Cell: 20 °C
					Row:
						Cell: Evening · 17:00–23:00
							Row header: true
						Cell: 21.5 °C
						Cell: 21.5 °C
					Row:
						Cell: Night · 23:00–06:30
							Row header: true
						Cell: 16 °C
						Cell: 16 °C
			Heading 2:
				Text: Troubleshooting
			Markdown:
				Table columns: auto
				Content >>
					| Symptom | Probable cause | What to do |
					|---------|----------------|-----------|
					| The screen does not turn on | No power or a loose wire | Check the electrical panel and terminals L and N |
					| Status light in red | It cannot connect to the Wi-Fi network | Move the router closer or repeat the pairing |
					| The boiler does not start | C/NO contact wired wrong | Check the diagram on page {page of: wiring} |
					| Wrong temperature | It is near a heat source | Move it to another spot, 1.5 m from the floor |
			Heading 2:
				Id: specs-heading
				Text: Technical specifications
			Table:
				Id: specs
				Column sizes: 150 *
				Body:
					Row:
						Cell: Power supply
							Row header: true
						Cell: 230 V AC, 50 Hz, or 2 AA batteries
							Style: mono
					Row:
						Cell: Output contact
							Row header: true
						Cell: 6 A / 250 V, potential-free
							Style: mono
					Row:
						Cell: Temperature range
							Row header: true
						Cell: 5 to 30 °C, in 0.5 °C steps
							Style: mono
					Row:
						Cell: Connectivity
							Row header: true
						Cell: Wi-Fi 2.4 GHz (IEEE 802.11 b/g/n)
							Style: mono
					Row:
						Cell: Dimensions
							Row header: true
						Cell: 86 × 86 × 24 mm
							Style: mono
		Block:
			Id: support
			Heading 2:
				Text: Warranty and support
			Columns:
				Count: 2
				Gap: 26
				Separator: 0.5
				Separator color: #BFD9D7
				Box:
					Margin: 0 0 12 0
				Markdown:
					Content >>
						### Warranty

						The Aire+ T2 has a **three-year** warranty from the date of purchase, covering any manufacturing defect. It does not cover damage from incorrect installation or damage caused by moisture or impacts. Keep the invoice: we will ask for it to process the warranty.

						### Recycling

						At the end of its useful life, do not throw the thermostat away with household waste. Take it to a recycling center or hand it in at any store when you buy a new one. Batteries are recycled separately.
